 every question in the prep doc. Open any section in your browser — diagrams use Mermaid CDN where present.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"study-order\">\n      <strong>Suggested order:</strong> 01 Streaming → 02 Conversation state → 03 MCP → 04 Artifacts → 10 Killer questions → rest.\n      <p class=\"study-hint\">Each section page now includes <strong>interactive demos</strong>, <strong>flashcard mode</strong>, and <strong>study progress tracking</strong> (saved in your browser). Open any section and use “Mark as studied” to track review.</p>\n      <p class=\"study-hint\"><a href=\"../claude-frontend-architecture.html\"><strong>Interactive architecture map</strong></a> — full-system diagram with layer filters, flow walkthroughs, and links to every section.</p>\n      <p class=\"study-hint\"><a href=\"../claude-system-design-interview.html\"><strong>Interview template (45–60m)</strong></a> — full answer in Requirements → Architecture → Data Model → API/BFF → Deep Dive format.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <ul class=\"sections\">\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"01-streaming-real-time-rendering.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 1</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Streaming &amp; Real-Time Rendering</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">10 questions · Markdown, SSE, throttling, backpressure</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"02-conversation-state-management.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 2</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Conversation State Management</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">10 questions · Branching, sync, context window</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"03-mcp-tool-use-ui.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 3</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">MCP &amp; Tool Use UI</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">11 questions · Tool pills, idempotency, trust boundary</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"04-artifacts-sandboxed-rendering.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 4</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Artifacts &amp; Sandboxed Rendering</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">11 questions · iframe sandbox, CSP, versioning</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"05-performance-scalability.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 5</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Performance &amp; Scalability</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">11 questions · Virtualization, TTFT, caching</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"06-auth-security-multitenancy.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 6</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Auth, Security &amp; Multitenancy</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">10 questions · RLS, org isolation, MCP audit</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"07-offline-resilience-error-handling.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 7</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Offline, Resilience &amp; Error Handling</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">9 questions · Reconnect, resume stream, degraded mode</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"08-input-multimodal-ux.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 8</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Input &amp; Multimodal UX</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">9 questions · Uploads, slash commands, voice</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"09-api-design-provider-abstraction.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 9</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">API Design &amp; Provider Abstraction</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">8 questions · Anthropic vs OpenAI, streaming adapter</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <a href=\"10-killer-questions.html\">\n          <div class=\"num\">Section 10</div>\n          <div class=\"title\">Killer Questions</div>\n          <div class=\"meta\">6 multi-system scenarios · Full mini-design docs</div>\n        </a>\n      </li>\n